    "ExplanationWrongA": "",
    "ExplanationWrongB": "Prioritizing liquidity ratios while disregarding the 2.8× debt-to-equity ratio and 0.12 operating cash flow coverage is inconsistent with fundamental credit analysis. For a retailer facing a projected 4–6% industry contraction, strong current and quick ratios — which depend heavily on inventory values that become uncertain in a downturn — do not protect against solvency risk. High leverage with thin cash flow coverage threatens the entity's ability to meet obligations even when working capital appears ample. A candidate selecting this option commits the error of treating ratio analysis as a single-dimension exercise.",
